label chapter_one:

    scene bg classroom

    narrator "Three days later."
    narrator "New chapter."
    narrator "New board notes."

    narrator "He's already remembered everything by the time you've uncapped your pen."

    mc "Chapter 12. Electrostatistics."
    rival "Electric Charges and Fields."

    rival "The chapter is called {i}Electric Charges and Fields.{/i}"
    rival "Not Electrostatics."

    narrator "You stare at him."

    mc "Are you serious right now."

    rival "Precision."

    mc "Whatever."

    narrator "You go through the first twenty minutes understanding nothing."
    narrator "Then the teacher writes Columb's Law on the board in four minutes flat."

    mc "(That's it? That's the whole explanation?)"

    scene bg library
    
    orion "Let's start from the beginning."
    orion "What's a charge?"
    mc "A property of matter. Positive or negative."
    orion "More specific."
    mc "It's a fundamental scalar quantity of matter that causes it to experience a force when placed in an electromagnetic field."
    orion "Good. Where does the word electricity come from?"
    mc "Greek. {i}Elecktron.{/i} Amber."
    orion "Why amber?"
    mc "Because rubbing it creates static electricity."
    mc "The Greeks noticed."
    orion "Right."
    narrator "He writes something in the margin of his notebook."
    narrator "You try to read it upside down."
    narrator "You can't."

    mc "What are you writing?"

    orion "What you get right."

    mc "Okay my turn to ask you!"

    mc "Three properties of charges. Go."

    orion "Quantization, additivity, conservation."

    mc "Define quantization."

    orion "Total charge (q) of a body is a multiple of e in discrete amounts."
    orion "You can't half a charge."

    mc "Additivity"

    orion "Total charge of the system is the algebraic solution of individual charges loacated at different points inside the system."

    mc "Conservation"

    orion "1. The total charge of an isolated system remains constant."
    orion "2. The electric charges can neither be created nor destroyed, they can only be transferred from one body to another."

    orion "My turn."
    mc "Why does your smile look sinister?"

    return

